'''Kis''' is an [[Oceanic language]] of [[East Sepik Province]] in [[Papua New Guinea]]. It is spoken to the southeast of Samap village ({{coord|-3.737823|143.933158|type:city_region:PG|name=Samap 1}}) in [[Turubu Rural LLG]], [[East Sepik Province]].

